SEP boot fix: GET_STATUS handshake before TZ0 (and before IMG4).

MacFingerprint Touch ID RE. Kernel AsahiLinux/linux asahi-7.1.5-2 (drivers/soc/apple/sep.rs).
Applies AFTER sep-discover-log / sep-trace-rx / sep-trace-tx (replaces the old
sep-getrand-probe + sep-cpu-reset survey patches).

Root cause (proven live on an M1/t8103 via m1n1 proxy hw/sep.py): the SEP boot ROM
answers the boot protocol, but m1n1s working boot() pings GET_STATUS (type 0x2) and
waits for STATUS_OK (0x66) BEFORE sending TZ0 (and again before IMG4). The Asahi stub
fired TZ0 blind -> the ROM stayed silent. This adds the two-stage GET_STATUS handshake:
start() sends GET_STATUS; on STATUS_OK send TZ0; on TZ0_ACK2 send GET_STATUS again;
on the 2nd STATUS_OK load firmware + shmem (IMG4 / SET_SHMEM as before).

